{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-70895" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,-5,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=4-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-70895" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-5,-2⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=4-t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨2,3,4⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨-3,4,-1⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-3,4,-1⟩,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-3,4,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ & =⟨3,-5,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-70895" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8b4058e6ad4d11c59444d5e560a5ee7d97491e0039706319ee0f41b2fbb700b"} {"question" "q-70895" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-70895" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩=-27"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩=0"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩=⟨3,-5,-2⟩"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,-2⟩=-27"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,-2⟩=⟨-3,4,-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-70895" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩=-27"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-3,1,-2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ -3{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8b4058e6ad4d11c59444d5e560a5ee7d97491e0039706319ee0f41b2fbb700b"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩=\\sqrt{7}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩=\\sqrt{7}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-1,1,3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩ & =0 \\\\ -{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1} & ={t}_{2}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{2},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨3,\\,0,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8b4058e6ad4d11c59444d5e560a5ee7d97491e0039706319ee0f41b2fbb700b"} {"question" "q-127910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\sqrt{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1)$, we can find a vector that is parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,-3,1⟩-⟨4,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨3,-4,4⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =⟨1,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8b4058e6ad4d11c59444d5e560a5ee7d97491e0039706319ee0f41b2fbb700b"} {"question" "q-127927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-4,-4,3⟩=11"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,4⟩=12"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩=23"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨3,4,4⟩=23"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,4⟩=11"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩=23"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f8f6c5bbe9902262ba448030d1b872ab8157dcf3e5a130c69d67c94323dc64a"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-3,2,1)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "fil